# ${{skill.name}} — Vault `${{instance.name}}` (${{config.base_url}})

Run from anywhere (do not explore script paths; use `--help` if needed):

`${{driver.python}} ${{driver.cli}} --instance ${{instance.name}} <command>`

## Hard rules
- **Metadata only.** NEVER read, print or ask for secret values. The CLI refuses `/data/`, `/creds/`, `/decrypt/`, `/sign/`, `/read`, unwrap, `sys/raw`, cubbyhole and anything not on its metadata allow-list, before sending. If it refuses, tell the user why; never work around it (no curl, no `vault kv get`, no other tools).
- No writes in this version. Token comes from the integration config; never print, echo or `cat` it.
- If the user means another Vault, use that instance's skill.

## Commands
| Need | Command |
|---|---|
| Connection check (config, health, token, mounts) | `test` |
| Active/standby/sealed, version | `health`, `seal-status` |
| Auth methods / secret engines (type, KV version) | `auth-methods`, `mounts` |
| ACL policies / policy text | `policies`, `policies <name>` |
| Secret path names (keys only) | `ls <mount/path> [--limit N=200]` |
| KV v2 versions, created/updated, custom metadata (no data) | `meta <mount/path>` |
| Own token policies/ttl/expiry | `whoami` |
| Does my token have access to a path? (reads nothing) | `caps <path> [<path>...]` |
| Leases below a prefix | `leases <prefix> [--within H] [--limit N=100]`, `leases --count` |
| Audit devices | `audit` |
| Other allow-listed metadata endpoint | `raw GET\|LIST <path>` |

Bound scans: use specific prefixes and `--limit`; lease listing needs `sys/leases` policy (403 = not permitted).

## Watchers (`watch_script`, `watcher=<recipe>`, `integration=${{instance.name}}`; scripts in `${{driver.watch_dir}}`)
| Recipe | Fires when | Flags |
|---|---|---|
| `vault-health` | Vault becomes sealed / uninitialized / unreachable, or recovers | — |
| `vault-token-expiry` | the instance token expires within N days (once per token) | `--days D` (default 7) |
| `vault-lease-expiry` | leases under a prefix expire within N hours (each once) | `--prefix P` (required), `--hours H` (default 24), `--limit N` |

First run records a baseline. Always run with `dry_run` first and report clearly whether it was a dry run or a registered watch.
